<TEI xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0" xml:id="CH2b1559-en-18cfe757" type="transl"><teiHeader><fileDesc><titleStmt><title>Draft translation of 聲無哀樂論</title><editor role="translator">Christoph Harbsmeier</editor></titleStmt><publicationStmt><ab>published electronically as part of the TLS project at https://hxwd.org</ab><availability status="2"><ab>This work has been licensed for use in the TLS</ab></availability></publicationStmt><sourceDesc><bibl><title>Draft translation of 聲無哀樂論</title>Draft: Oxford, 1971</bibl><ab>Translation of <bibl corresp="#CH2b1559"><title xml:lang="och"/></bibl> into <lang xml:lang="en">English</lang>.</ab></sourceDesc></fileDesc><profileDesc><creation resp="#CH">Initially created: <date>2026-05-10T21:05:56.502+09:00</date> by CH</creation></profileDesc></teiHeader><text><body><div><head>Translated parts</head><p xml:id="CH2b1559-start"><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.59" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T00:22:36.701+09:00">So then: the Music says this; the Music says that,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.60" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T00:32:04.919+09:00">is there no more to it than bells and drums (and no more)? [Music is more than the bells and drums that express it.]</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.61" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T00:23:53.965+09:00">Grief speaks of this, Grief speaks of that,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.62" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T00:32:53.359+09:00">is there no more to it than wailing and weeping? [Grief is more than its expression in wailing and weeping!</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.63" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T00:36:28.282+09:00">Speaking along these lines</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.64" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T00:37:49.348+09:00">jade and silk are not the substance of ritual (and?) deference</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.65" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T00:44:26.518+09:00">song and dance performance is not the main point of mourning.</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.66" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T00:45:06.742+09:00">How is one to make all this plain?</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.67" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T00:46:22.444+09:00">So: different regions have different customs:</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.68" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T00:48:18.979+09:00">their chanting and wailing is not the same.</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.69" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T01:02:51.617+09:00">When used in complex contexts</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.70" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T01:03:14.87+09:00">some will hear wailing and feel elated,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.71" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T01:11:02.719+09:00">others will hear singing and feel dejected,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.72" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T01:12:02.008+09:00">and yet their feelings of grief and joy are quite the same.</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.73" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T01:12:30.414+09:00">Now if on the basis of quite the same feelings</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.74" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T01:13:07.62+09:00">one emits vastly different sounds,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.75" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T01:15:28.515+09:00">is this not because the sound of music is not emotionally constant?</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.76" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T01:24:06.405+09:00">And yet the harmonious juxtaposition of musical tones</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.77" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T01:24:49.819+09:00">is what affects humans most profoundly.</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.78" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T01:26:39.863+09:00">toiling workers sing songs to their work,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.79" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T01:29:51.532+09:00">those pleased with themselves celebrate their feats through dances.</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.80" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T01:31:53.835+09:00">And so those who suffer sad pain in their hearts</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.81" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T01:34:28.541+09:00">will come up with acutely sorrowful words.</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.82" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T01:35:15.87+09:00">Words properly aligned become songs,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.83" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T01:36:11.125+09:00">sounds properly aligned become music:</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.84" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T01:38:11.79+09:00">one mixes these together to intone them,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.85" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T01:38:29.503+09:00">and one gathers to listen to them.</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.86" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T01:39:27.144+09:00">The mind gets moved by sounds in harmony,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.87" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T01:42:10.388+09:00">and empathy is aroused by bitter words:</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.88" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T01:43:21.463+09:00">but before the sighs grow still</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.89" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T01:44:55.471+09:00">the tears are cascading.</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.90" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T01:45:23.446+09:00">The mourning heart stays hidden inside,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.91" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T01:49:05.708+09:00">only when exposed to harmonious musical cadence it comes to light. </seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.92" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T01:53:25.07+09:00">The harmonious musical cadence is formlessly present,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.93" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T01:55:55.9+09:00">whereas the mournful heart belong to a host.</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.94" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T01:57:25.552+09:00">So then, with a mournful heart belonging to a host</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.95" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T01:58:20.233+09:00">basing oneself on a formlessly present harmonious musical cadence,</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.96" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T01:58:55.731+09:00">what one is struck by</seg><seg corresp="#CH2b1559_CHANT_005-1a.97" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-05-12T01:59:38.048+09:00">is only mournful grief, that is all.</seg></p></div></body></text></TEI>